                        ],
                        "form": "комбата́нте"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "57680f88-584c-4fe2-acfe-bf37cb35d021",
                        "entry_id": "699a39b8-d400-3d22-8b8a-831065062933",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "комбата́нтах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a30a5e9a-8a85-3a12-be07-69e2eab9f3d3",
                        "entry_id": "699a39b8-d400-3d22-8b8a-831065062933",
                        "glosses": [
                            "юр., дипл., : лицо, входящее в состав вооружённых сил воюющей стороны и непосредственно принимающее участие в военных действиях"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "в международном праве"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "985146d1-894f-493b-b7f5-08459622ffdd",
                                "sense_id": "a30a5e9a-8a85-3a12-be07-69e2eab9f3d3",
                                "text": "В одном из официальных документов, в качестве препятствия к принятию её, приводилось то соображение, что в случае несчастия с её аппаратом на театре военных действий, она, попав в неприятельский стан, будет сочтена, как женщина, не комбатантом, а шпионом, и, поэтому, должна подлежать смертной казни."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f5ae8df-c4d6-43db-9ee2-09531335199a",
                                "sense_id": "a30a5e9a-8a85-3a12-be07-69e2eab9f3d3",
                                "text": "Военкорам в эти дни выдавали автоматы. Принципа несовместимости статусов комбатанта и журналиста, принятого сегодня, тогда никто бы просто не понял."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a48a394c-1670-45fb-ae6d-8c501a1eaed7",
                                "sense_id": "a30a5e9a-8a85-3a12-be07-69e2eab9f3d3",
                                "text": "Для того, чтобы обосновать квалификацию Аль-Муджахира как комбатанта противной стороны, американской администрации придётся доказать в гражданском суде наличие явной связи между его деятельностью и вооружённым конфликтом в Афганистане с участием США."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27883986-a609-3565-82c8-c63d38def848",
                        "entry_id": "699a39b8-d400-3d22-8b8a-831065062933",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. соперник, противник"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "499ef65f-fb00-4704-bd73-b703795401ff",
                                "sense_id": "27883986-a609-3565-82c8-c63d38def848",
                                "text": "Никогда ещё во Франции избирательная борьба не велась с таким ожесточением и упорством и при участии такого огромнаго количества комбатантов."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f30a658a-2f01-45b1-ba0a-adf8f940c9f3",
                                "sense_id": "27883986-a609-3565-82c8-c63d38def848",
                                "text": "«Он», — вскрикнул Мильдью и бросился вперёд, но тотчас же вспомнил, что по дуэльному кодексу комбатантам говорить друг с другом воспрещено .."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90a9a82a-7778-4ae4-8d1d-6990715f9299",
                        "source_entry_id": "699a39b8-d400-3d22-8b8a-831065062933",
                        "target_lang_word": "combatant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "combatant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                        "entry_id": "9a8a0859-051d-379a-ba71-067455a32542",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person engaged in combat, often armed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0036dd2f-d2f3-46e1-81c4-0275e1ddf124",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "Gladiators were combatants who fought to the death to entertain the public."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c68765b-9c74-4ac4-b8f6-e07e87738354",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "Come hither, you that would be combatants:\nHenceforth I charge you, as you love our favour,\nQuite to forget this quarrel and the cause."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82a2d682-c7f8-4368-9026-5b501d84a827",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "On the passage, one day, for the diversion of those gentlemen, all the boys were called on the quarter deck, and were paired proportionably, and then made to fight; after which the gentlemen gave the combatants from five to nine shillings each."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45b8894c-b0e7-4401-a1b4-dc4a474b9486",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "If any combatant was struck down, and unable to recover his feet, his squire or page might enter the lists, and drag his master out of the press; but in that case the knight was adjudged vanquished […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eef67ffd-ba17-4d8e-ab57-1a03e62ef665",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "“[…] Don’t you realize that alcohol is an essential part of heroism? The combatant and the drunkard are brothers, you genius.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a96a7236-845c-4e56-b3fb-e80ca2eaf1aa",
                                                "sense_id": "d89ec98a-b534-3681-bb35-74e8264fba7b",
                                                "text": "The leading voices of the womanosphere are using a similar strategy. As Brittany Hugoboom put it in an op–ed for the rightwing outlet Quillette: “Conservatives will never win if they imagine themselves as combatants atop defensive battlements, hurling abuse on the mass media. We need to involve ourselves in the creation of pop culture.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "combatant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "133809cd-de03-361b-9d40-6dc3485257f7",
                                        "entry_id": "555f0e46-0622-3e8a-96ab-6dbfc659232d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contending; disposed to contend."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "963ab559-5df4-4b0c-829b-0ac7bd46c081",
                                                "sense_id": "133809cd-de03-361b-9d40-6dc3485257f7",
                                                "text": "Their valours are not yet so combatant,\nOr truly antagonistick, as to fight;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "428ce5c4-e131-34a2-a6c5-db6fa8bff2b9",
                                        "entry_id": "555f0e46-0622-3e8a-96ab-6dbfc659232d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Involving combat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a8c02a3-fac1-4d1f-9796-dbb4082572cb",
                                                "sense_id": "428ce5c4-e131-34a2-a6c5-db6fa8bff2b9",
                                                "text": "He wished he were in a combatant service; he wanted to fight, fight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07b8d6ed-ea7c-399b-a414-a9b4933f7c03",
                                        "entry_id": "555f0e46-0622-3e8a-96ab-6dbfc659232d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of combattant (“in heraldry: in a fighting position”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd7029ca-d1ee-434d-a66b-ee194c726cb9",
                                                "sense_id": "07b8d6ed-ea7c-399b-a414-a9b4933f7c03",
                                                "text": "Or, two lions combatant gules, armed and langued (that is, claws and tongue) azure, is borne by the name of Wycombe; Azure , two lions combatant or, by the name of Carter; Azure , two lions combatant guardant argent, by […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "446be85a-3ae6-4b47-aee5-ef104a37b729",
                        "source_entry_id": "699a39b8-d400-3d22-8b8a-831065062933",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kombattant",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kombattant",
